                  "key": "gen_ai.output.messages",
                  "value": {
                    "stringValue": "[{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"parts\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"content\":\"An **agent trace** is a chronological record of what an AI agent did while completing a task. It may include the agent’s inputs and outputs, tool calls and their results, handoffs to other agents, timing, and errors.\\n\\nFor example, a trace for “find the weather and suggest what to wear” might show:\\n\\n1. User asks for a recommendation.\\n2. Agent calls a weather tool.\\n3. Tool returns the forecast.\\n4. Agent replies with a clothing suggestion.\\n\\nTraces help developers debug behavior, measure performance, and understand where a task went wrong. They generally record observable actions—not necessarily the model’s private internal reasoning.\"}],\"finish_reason\":\"stop\"}]"
